<script module>
  import Demo from "$ui/components/Demo.abide"
  import StateDemo from "$ui/demos/templating/reactivity/StateDemo.abide"
  import ComputedDemo from "$ui/demos/templating/reactivity/ComputedDemo.abide"
  import LinkedDemo from "$ui/demos/templating/reactivity/LinkedDemo.abide"
  import WatchSourceDemo from "$ui/demos/templating/reactivity/WatchSourceDemo.abide"
  import WatchThunkDemo from "$ui/demos/templating/reactivity/WatchThunkDemo.abide"
  import SharedTallyDemo from "$ui/demos/templating/reactivity/SharedTallyDemo.abide"
</script>

<main class="page">
  <h1>Reactive primitives</h1>
  <p class="lead">Every reactive primitive, one concept per card. A <code>state</code> is a writable cell that drives fine-grained updates; a <code>computed</code> derives from it lazily; a <code>linked</code> cell reseeds when its source changes; and two flavours of <code>watch</code> push side effects — one change-only, one auto-tracked. Under each live demo is the exact source that powers it — read live from disk and highlighted on the server.</p>

  <Demo id="state" title="<code>state(v, transform?)</code> — writable cell" client="src/ui/demos/templating/reactivity/StateDemo.abide">
    <StateDemo />
  </Demo>

  <Demo id="computed" title="<code>state.computed</code> — derived cell" client="src/ui/demos/templating/reactivity/ComputedDemo.abide">
    <ComputedDemo />
  </Demo>

  <Demo id="linked" title="<code>state.linked</code> — reseeding writable cell" client="src/ui/demos/templating/reactivity/LinkedDemo.abide">
    <LinkedDemo />
  </Demo>

  <Demo id="watch-source" title="<code>watch(source, handler)</code> — change-only effect" client="src/ui/demos/templating/reactivity/WatchSourceDemo.abide">
    <WatchSourceDemo />
  </Demo>

  <Demo id="watch-thunk" title="<code>watch(thunk)</code> — auto-tracked effect" client="src/ui/demos/templating/reactivity/WatchThunkDemo.abide">
    <WatchThunkDemo />
  </Demo>

  <p>Two separate component instances call <code>state.shared("reactivity-tally", 0)</code> with the SAME key, so they share one backing state — bump either and both update. The value also syncs across other open tabs of this app (via a <code>BroadcastChannel</code>).</p>

  <Demo id="shared" title="<code>state.shared(key, initial)</code> — cell shared by key" client="src/ui/demos/templating/reactivity/SharedTallyDemo.abide">
    <SharedTallyDemo />
  </Demo>
</main>
